::scene COLD_OPEN

ROOM zone_studio_1782953094650

EVENT FADE_IN

TITLE vital_encore_logo

MUSIC vital_encore_jingle
♪ A warm, syrupy jingle swells — the kind that plays in waiting rooms where nobody leaves. ♪
MUSIC_END

CAM 1 WIDE showroom_floor

SHOT
A showroom of clone vats stretches into the dark, each one lit from beneath like a display case. Something turns over slowly inside the nearest tank.
SHOT_END

NARRATOR:
You died last Tuesday.

WAIT 1.5

NARRATOR:
Statistically, you will die again before the weekend.

NARRATOR:
The question was never IF you come back. The question is: who's paying for it?

::scene THE_PITCH

CAM 2 MEDIUM pitchman_mark

ENTER npc_marv_sallow

ACTION npc_marv_sallow spreads his arms wide, sleeves damp, grinning with roughly nine too many teeth.

MARV:
Friend. Neighbour. Statistical inevitability. Marv Sallow, VITAL ENCORE™.

MARV:
Right now, if your heart stops in this city, you wake up in a municipal vat with a stranger's dental records and a bill for the electricity.

ACTION npc_marv_sallow leans in until the lens fogs.

MARV:
That's not a comeback. That's a clerical error with a pulse.

TITLE vital_encore_tiers

MARV:
For less than you spend on synthetic breakfast, we keep a YOU on file. Fresh. Filed. Ready to walk.

::scene TESTIMONIAL

CAM 3 CLOSEUP testimonial_chair

LOWER_THIRD
DEB OKONKWO
SATISFIED CUSTOMER — LIKENESS APPROXIMATE
LOWER_THIRD_END

ENTER npc_deb_okonkwo

ACTION npc_deb_okonkwo sits very still. She has not blinked since the camera cut to her.

DEB:
I've been with Encore since my third body.

DEB:
This is my seventh. It's my favourite so far. The hands are nearly right.

ACTION npc_deb_okonkwo looks down at her hands for slightly too long.

DEB:
I don't remember my mother's face anymore. But that was the Bronze tier. That's on me.

MARV:
Ha ha! Deb, everybody. Living proof.

ACTION npc_marv_sallow claps her on the shoulder. She does not move.

::scene THE_CLOSE

CAM 1 WIDE showroom_floor

NARRATOR:
VITAL ENCORE™. Because the worst thing that can happen to you isn't dying.

NARRATOR:
It's dying uninsured.

OVERLAY
CALL NOW — COLDWATER 7-7-ENCORE

FIRST BACKUP FREE WITH ANY CORPSE

OPERATORS ARE STANDING. NOT NECESSARILY BY. JUST STANDING.
OVERLAY_END

TICKER
VITAL ENCORE™ is a wholly owned subsidiary of itself · Continuity of consciousness is a marketing term and not a guarantee · Backups older than 90 days may exhibit drift, gaps, or opinions the original did not hold · Restored persons are legally distinct from the deceased and may not inherit, marry, or testify · Do not restore more than one copy simultaneously; if this occurs, VITAL ENCORE™ will determine which is you · That determination is final · Side effects include phantom memory, vat lung, and the persistent sense of being slightly behind
TICKER_END

WAIT 3

CAM 2 MEDIUM pitchman_mark

MARV:
Don't let the city decide what you come back as.

ACTION npc_marv_sallow winks. It takes his whole face.

MARV:
Come back as YOU. Ish.

MUSIC vital_encore_jingle
♪ The jingle returns, warmer and slower, resolving on a chord that doesn't quite land. ♪
MUSIC_END

